WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:02.180
(intense music)

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.780
- In Kabul streets are full of life.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.930
Markets are busy and even amusement parks

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.450
are open for visitors,

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.460
including some bemused Taliban fighters.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.800
This street in the Afghan capital Kabul

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.570
used to be closed for most
Afghan citizens until recently,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.290
this is where the Afghan
ministry of interior used to be

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.400
and where the European union's
mission was also located.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.290
That meant that you get into the street,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.680
you had to pass several
layers of security barriers.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.620
Those barriers have now been taken down

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.830
as the Taliban try to
convey a sense of normalcy

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.703
in the capital.

00:00:36.024 --> 00:00:39.107
- (foreign language)

00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:47.150
- But the situation here
is far from back to normal.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.720
The economy is on the verge of collapse

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.560
and many Afghans say they don't know

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.340
where the next paycheck
is gonna come from.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.150
And it's not just the economy.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.610
Women's freedoms are being taken away.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.810
The Taliban have banned teenage
girls from going to school

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.660
and reintroduced harsh
Islamic punishments,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.480
as they shot, and then hung a group of

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.140
alleged kidnappers in Herat.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:08.973
So in many ways,

00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:11.020
the reality on the ground here in Kabul

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.990
is in contrast to the messages

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.740
that the Taliban have been sending.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.890
Since the Taliban took control in August,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.770
fighters have been patrolling the streets,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.463
toting guns and Manning
checkpoints in Kabul.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.160
Their presence demonstrates
military might,

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.130
but it's also a way for
the Taliban to convey

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.530
that Afghans are safe.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.613
- (foreign language)

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.470
- But a recent spate of attacks

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.593
is undermining that sense of security.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.320
In Kabul a bomb exploded at
a mosque in early October,

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.270
leaving several citizens dead.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.120
No one immediately claimed
responsibility for the attack.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.240
In other parts of the country,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.580
the Taliban had been struggling
to contain the threat

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.080
from Islamic state,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.733
which has said it was behind
deadly roadside bombings.

00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:05.816
- (foreign language)

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:22.500
- Both the Taliban and Islamic state

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.570
want to impose strict
Islamic rules on Afghanistan,

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:28.940
but have deep religious
and political differences.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.390
The Taliban have been trying
to portray a moderate image,

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.450
but on the ground, they've
reimposed harsh punishments,

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.560
reminiscent of how they
used to rule the country

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.270
in the late 1990s.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.790
In the Western city of Herat,

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.260
the Taliban killed four men

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.380
they accused of being kidnappers.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.180
Then hung them from a public square.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.330
Many Afghans fear the
Taliban's hard-line rule,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.700
especially those who worry

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.620
that it will threaten basic freedoms.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.703
- (foreign language)

00:03:04.521 --> 00:03:06.360
- Women in particular have borne the brunt

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.470
of these new regulations.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:09.910
The Taliban initially said

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.343
that it will allow women to attend school.

00:03:12.343 --> 00:03:15.426
- (foreign language)

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.530
- But we've seen now

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.350
that they've banned girls from
attending secondary school

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.740
and women have been
sent home from offices.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.520
In many provinces of the country,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.970
women are no longer
allowed to leave the house

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:40.033
without a male relative escorting
them around the streets.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.300
Many Afghans fear that
the Taliban will ban music

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.013
like the date in the 1990s.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.960
Already many Afghans refrain
from playing music in public

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.860
and classes have stopped at the renowned

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.560
National Institute of Music,

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.982
which was home to the country's
first, all female orchestra

00:03:57.982 --> 00:04:01.065
- (foreign language)

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.470
- As they work out how to govern,

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.440
the Taliban have been seeking

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.080
to woo the international community

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.710
and win diplomatic recognition.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.610
However, most countries have stopped short

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.110
of officially recognizing
the Taliban's government

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.920
and have suspended aid.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.300
After the Taliban took control,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.610
the US, the IMF and other countries

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.970
also froze Afghanistan's
foreign currency reserves,

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.040
which the country is heavily reliant on.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.520
And that's had a huge
effect on the economy.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.940
There's a lack of cash

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.620
and banks have put a strict limit

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.980
on how much money people can withdraw.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.410
That means Afghans don't have enough money

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.170
to buy the food that they used to,

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.830
and they don't have enough money

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.973
to basically keep the economy going.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.280
Before the Taliban came to power,

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.010
nearly half the population
lived in poverty,

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.180
but it was rare to see scenes like this,

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.230
of Afghans struggling to find food

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.870
or queuing up outside
ATMs to withdraw cash.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.320
The UN has warned of growing starvation

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.862
and pledged 1.2 billion in emergency aid.

00:05:06.862 --> 00:05:09.945
- (foreign language)

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.460
- Many people who work
for the former government

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.920
had lost their jobs.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.100
Unemployment is soaring

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.010
and at the same time, prices
of food and fuel are rising,

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.510
and Afghans are worried
that the coming winter

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.853
is going to be a struggle.

